36 Days. One account. Zero warnings. Zero humans. Zero replies to 40 emails.

My Instagram @iamkaizaadbanaji was suspended on October 19 after a cyber attack. 

While the account was already locked, @Meta allowed the unauthorised user to remove my own number from my own account . That is not security. That is a punchline.

Not after a low-risk warning.  Not after a medium-risk notice.  Not after a final strike.  

@Meta own policy has a ladder. Three warnings before suspension. I never saw a single rung.

Three grievance tickets filed. Three closed with no resolution. One still pending since November 12.  @Meta Verified  paid for  returns the same automated maze.  

40 emails. Zero replies.

Under India’s IT Rules 2021, a Grievance Officer must acknowledge a complaint within 24 hours and resolve it within 15 days.  
It has been 36 days now

@mosseri  you said Instagram stands for real people and real accountability.   Prove it.  

Restore the account or publicly explain why a cyber-attack victim gets less process than a Terms of Service footnote.

@instagram this is your platform. Your policy. Your silence.

@alexandr_wang  your so-called AI at @Meta cannot tell a real person from a threat and is deleting accounts with zero communication. Fix the system or own the failure. Enough is enough.

This is not moderation. This is a company that skipped every safeguard it wrote and is now betting silence will outlast accountability.

@Meta @instagram @mosseri @kunalb11 @finkd @alexandr_wang  restore @iamkaizaadbanaji or answer in public why an Indian user gets no process at all.

#MetaFail #36Days #HumanReviewNow #GrievanceOfficerSilent

